{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #1013: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. Let $h_3(k)$ be the minimal $n$ such that there exists a triangle-free graph on $n$ vertices with chromatic number $k$. Find an asymptotic for $h_3(k)$, and also prove\\[\\lim_{k\\to \\infty}\\frac{h_3(k+1)}{h_3(k)}=1.\\] Current best: It is known that\\[\\frac{\\log k}{\\log\\log k}k^2 \\ll h_3(k) \\ll (\\log k)k^2.\\]The lower bound is due to Graver and Yackel \\cite{GrYa68}, the upper bound follows from Shearer's upper bound for $R(3,k)$ (see [165]). The function $h_r(k)$ for $r\\geq 4$ is the subject of [920]. Prize: no. OEIS: A292528. Tags: graph theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_93005904c9c2d844e661449b2b76aaf15895a90349e99c5b46d4ca9992fed64f","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:1013","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_930b2fa51f57df3b","object_root":"sha256:ad05f459a8fe39e93db74c207ab236bf46911e4620af509d718c65ffb6d39555","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"datab